# Jetnity Traveller Context Intelligence – Always Apply

For every new or changed Jetnity feature, explicitly check whether the result can materially differ by traveller context such as multiple citizenships, multiple travel documents/credentials, issuing country, residence, route/transit, or other necessary traveller-specific facts.

If relevant:

- do not silently use only one citizenship/pass/document when multiple legal options may exist;
- evaluate per traveller and per necessary legal credential option;
- keep Route Truth traveller-neutral and reusable;
- prefer legal/regulatory obligations over convenience;
- never invent visa, transit, health, carrier, eligibility or document rules;
- preserve `unknown` when evidence is insufficient;
- use progressive missing facts and data minimization;
- trigger stale/recheck only for domains actually affected by changed context;
- keep UX simple: primary valid/required option first, alternatives progressively disclosed;
- do not create product-specific shadow identity models.

If not relevant, do not collect or propagate traveller credentials unnecessarily.

